English (convenience translation; the German version prevails)
---------------------------------------------------------------

1. Scope. This license covers everything in this repository and on the pages published from
   it, except as set out in section 6: the Kern engine, Kern Studio, the Lehrer, the games and
   examples, the tools, the trained networks (in particular kern/policies/), levels, graphics,
   sounds, the documentation and the book (kern/docs/), and all files built from them
   (WebAssembly, JavaScript, HTML) – together "the Software".

2. Owner. All copyright, usage and other rights in the Software belong to Christian Heinrich
   Hohlfeld ("the Owner"). No rights are granted except those expressly named in section 3.

3. Permitted without a separate agreement is only: opening the publicly provided website in a
   browser and using the Software there for personal, non-commercial trying out.

4. Without the Owner's prior written consent it is in particular not permitted:
   a) to copy, reproduce, distribute, make publicly available, rent, sell or sublicense the
      Software or parts of it;
   b) to modify or translate it, create derivative works or incorporate parts into other
      software;
   c) to use it commercially or in any professional or business activity, including hosting,
      software as a service, embedding in products, robotics, simulation, training and running
      AI models, teaching and consulting;
   d) to use or pass on games exported with Studio or networks trained with the Lehrer beyond
      the use permitted in section 3;
   e) to use the Software, its documentation or its outputs to train, fine-tune or evaluate
      machine-learning models (text and data mining; the Owner expressly reserves this use
      under § 44b(3) of the German Copyright Act);
   f) to decompile, disassemble or otherwise reverse engineer the Software, except where
      mandatory law (§§ 69d, 69e UrhG) permits it;
   g) to remove or alter copyright notices, this license or markings.

5. Licenses for further uses, including commercial ones, are granted by the Owner separately
   and in writing on request.

6. Third-party components. The third-party components listed in kern/LICENSES.md (among them
   Box3D, Earcut, musl math, and the Micro Duck model, policies and meshes by Pollen Robotics)
   are governed solely by their own licenses (MIT, ISC, Apache 2.0; the Micro Duck meshes
   CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, i.e. non-commercial). This license does not
   restrict the rights in those components.

7. Warranty and liability. The Software is provided free of charge for trying out. The Owner
   is liable only for intent and gross negligence, under the German Product Liability Act, and
   for injury to life, body or health.

8. German law applies. If a provision is invalid, the rest remains in effect.
